---
layout: base.njk
---
{#- Sections-driven page (R-SEC-06 alternation, R-SEC-10 reveal below the fold, R-SEC-12 data only).
    Front matter: sections: [ "sample-id" | { type, … } ]; demote: true turns section h1s into h2s (style guide only).
    The page's computed breadcrumbs travel in ctx so page-header can show them (R-SEC-08). Any template body renders before the sections.
    Pages with a title open with a page-header built from title, eyebrow and lede unless their first section is a hero or page-header;
    front matter pageHeader: { variant: banner | band | split, image: { slug, alt, art, tone } } picks its picture variant (R-SEC-08).
    Case studies, events and jobs wrap their own sections in <article>, up to the first section that leads elsewhere (articleSplit). -#}
{% from "sections/_render.njk" import section with context %}
{{ content | safe }}
{%- set header = { eyebrow: eyebrow, title: title, lede: lede, variant: pageHeader.variant if pageHeader, image: pageHeader.image if pageHeader } if (title and not demote and not noHeader) else null -%}
{%- set steps = sections | sectionsPlan(locale, page.url, site.brand.density, demote, breadcrumbs, header) -%}
{%- if pageType in ["case-study", "event", "job"] %}
{%- set parts = steps | articleSplit %}
<article>
{%- for step in parts[0] %}
{{ section(step.s, step.ctx | merge({ inArticle: true })) }}
{%- endfor %}
</article>
{%- for step in parts[1] %}
{{ section(step.s, step.ctx) }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- else %}
{%- for step in steps %}
{{ section(step.s, step.ctx) }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
